<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  The Russian wording for the strings the native client owns.

  Product wording the web client also shows is generated into strings.xml for
  every locale from the shared locale files, so it has always been translated;
  the hand-written names here had no Russian at all, which is why a Russian
  phone showed English words in the middle of a translated screen.

  This file covers the task screen and the repeat editor — every string those
  two surfaces reach. The rest of strings_native.xml (sync, the unsent queue,
  settings, search, the account screens) still falls back to English and is
  worth a pass of its own.

  A name absent here falls back to values/strings_native.xml, which is why the
  priority codes P1..P4 and the em dash that stands in for an empty field are
  not repeated: they read the same in both languages.
-->
